WEBVTT

00:00:00.256 --> 00:00:03.413
Start with reviewed cluster-specific configuration files.

00:00:03.755 --> 00:00:07.723
Give them clear ordered names and keep the same cluster identity throughout.

00:00:07.979 --> 00:00:11.557
Each pipeline step pairs an action with its saved configuration.

00:00:11.807 --> 00:00:15.647
Keep passwords in separate credential references rather than in the files.

00:00:15.988 --> 00:00:18.356
Saving a pipeline does not execute it.

00:00:18.591 --> 00:00:22.388
Review every file against the installed framework schema before adding it to

00:00:22.431 --> 00:00:23.076
the sequence.

00:00:23.515 --> 00:00:27.099
Place a required initial administrator password change first.

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:31.024
Use the current credential to authorize it and a separate reference for the

00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:32.143
replacement credential.

00:00:32.494 --> 00:00:36.163
Verification must establish a fresh authenticated session with the new

00:00:36.206 --> 00:00:36.931
password.

00:00:37.188 --> 00:00:39.684
Later files must use that replacement reference.

00:00:40.004 --> 00:00:44.174
Leave password-change settings unused in later steps so they skip cleanly.

00:00:44.461 --> 00:00:48.173
Never repeat a completed password change simply because a subsequent step

00:00:48.301 --> 00:00:48.756
failed.

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:53.251
Use a narrowly reviewed configuration for EULA acceptance and the approved

00:00:53.421 --> 00:00:54.268
Pulse setting.

00:00:54.602 --> 00:00:59.615
Add the required D N S and N T P settings according to the installed schema.

00:00:59.935 --> 00:01:03.477
Check that later steps can authenticate and reach the cluster after the

00:01:03.519 --> 00:01:04.832
initial access changes.

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:08.962
Legal acceptance and telemetry settings are explicit organizational

00:01:09.175 --> 00:01:12.716
decisions; do not treat either as an automatic default for every

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:13.548
environment.

00:01:13.931 --> 00:01:18.283
Add supported virtual-machine networks, storage containers and any approved

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:19.883
high-availability settings.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:25.140
Review naming, V LANs, replication and capacity choices against the design.

00:01:25.554 --> 00:01:29.650
Verify the actual returned properties after creation, not only whether a

00:01:29.693 --> 00:01:31.122
container name exists.

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:35.111
Additional local administrators use their own credential references and

00:01:35.154 --> 00:01:36.168
explicit roles.

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:40.297
Check that every optional action is supported by the selected workflow and

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:41.164
target release.

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:46.014
Open Pipelines, create a descriptive name and add the saved actions in their

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:46.910
approved order.

00:01:47.209 --> 00:01:49.458
Select the exact file for each step.

00:01:49.701 --> 00:01:53.499
Review the password transition, targets and required approvals before

00:01:53.712 --> 00:01:54.267
saving.

00:01:54.608 --> 00:01:56.144
Steps execute sequentially.

00:01:56.443 --> 00:02:00.379
A failure stops later work; it does not roll back earlier changes.

00:02:00.817 --> 00:02:04.913
Approval-mandatory steps may require direct approved execution rather than

00:02:04.956 --> 00:02:06.492
unattended pipeline chaining.

00:02:06.919 --> 00:02:11.015
After execution, inspect every step and independently read back the

00:02:11.057 --> 00:02:12.175
requested settings.

00:02:12.483 --> 00:02:16.323
Verify new account access and both requested administrator roles.

00:02:16.664 --> 00:02:21.144
Before Prism Central registration, check its connectivity and trust, then

00:02:21.229 --> 00:02:23.843
confirm cluster identity and inventory there.

00:02:24.109 --> 00:02:28.504
If a step failed, reconcile the partial state and rerun only the pending

00:02:28.675 --> 00:02:30.403
action through a supported path.

00:02:30.723 --> 00:02:34.299
Preserve the successful jobs and final acceptance evidence.
